## Article 184. Judicial dispute resolution (grounds)

```catala
declaration scope Article184JudicialDisputeResolution:
  input resolution content JudicialDisputeResolution
  output canAppointResolution content YesNo

scope Article184JudicialDisputeResolution:
  label resolution_default definition canAppointResolution equals No

  label resolution_available exception resolution_default
  definition canAppointResolution under condition
    resolution.groundsExist = Yes
    and resolution.partiesConsent = Yes
    consequence equals Yes
```

## Article 185. Appointment of judicial dispute resolution

```catala
declaration scope Article185AppointmentResolution:
  input resolution content JudicialDisputeResolution
  output resolutionCanBeAppointed content YesNo

scope Article185AppointmentResolution:
  label appoint_default definition resolutionCanBeAppointed equals No

  label appoint_available exception appoint_default
  definition resolutionCanBeAppointed under condition
    resolution.groundsExist = Yes
    consequence equals Yes
```

## Article 186. Procedure for judicial dispute resolution

```catala
declaration scope Article186ResolutionProcedure:
  input resolution content JudicialDisputeResolution
  input partiesAttend content YesNo
  input mediatorAppointed content YesNo
  output resolutionProcedureValid content YesNo

scope Article186ResolutionProcedure:
  label procedure_default definition resolutionProcedureValid equals No

  label procedure_valid exception procedure_default
  definition resolutionProcedureValid under condition
    partiesAttend = Yes
    consequence equals Yes
```

## Article 187. Deadline for judicial dispute resolution

```catala
declaration scope Article187ResolutionDeadline:
  input resolution content JudicialDisputeResolution
  output resolutionDeadlineDays content integer

scope Article187ResolutionDeadline:
  label deadline definition resolutionDeadlineDays equals 30
```

## Article 188. Termination of judicial dispute resolution

```catala
declaration scope Article188TerminationResolution:
  input resolution content JudicialDisputeResolution
  input resolutionSuccessful content YesNo
  input deadlineExpired content YesNo
  input partyRequestsTermination content YesNo
  output resolutionMustTerminate content YesNo

scope Article188TerminationResolution:
  label terminate_default definition resolutionMustTerminate equals No

  label terminate_successful exception terminate_default
  definition resolutionMustTerminate under condition
    resolutionSuccessful = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label terminate_deadline exception terminate_default
  definition resolutionMustTerminate under condition
    deadlineExpired = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label terminate_request exception terminate_default
  definition resolutionMustTerminate under condition
    partyRequestsTermination = Yes
    consequence equals Yes
```

## Article 189. Withdrawal of claim and recognition of claim

```catala
declaration scope Article189WithdrawalRecognition:
  input plaintiffWithdrawsClaim content YesNo
  input defendantRecognizesClaim content YesNo
  input withdrawalVoluntary content YesNo
  input noViolationOfLaw content YesNo
  output withdrawalAccepted content YesNo
  output recognitionAccepted content YesNo

scope Article189WithdrawalRecognition:
  label withdrawal_default definition withdrawalAccepted equals No

  label withdrawal_accepted exception withdrawal_default
  definition withdrawalAccepted under condition
    plaintiffWithdrawsClaim = Yes
    and withdrawalVoluntary = Yes
    and noViolationOfLaw = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label recognition_default definition recognitionAccepted equals No

  label recognition_accepted exception recognition_default
  definition recognitionAccepted under condition
    defendantRecognizesClaim = Yes
    and noViolationOfLaw = Yes
    consequence equals Yes
```

## Article 190. Reconciliation of parties

```catala
declaration scope Article190Reconciliation:
  input reconciliation content ReconciliationProceeding
  input partiesAgree content YesNo
  input termsNotViolatingLaw content YesNo
  input termsNotViolatingOthersRights content YesNo
  output reconciliationCanBeApproved content YesNo

scope Article190Reconciliation:
  label reconcile_default definition reconciliationCanBeApproved equals No

  label reconcile_approved exception reconcile_default
  definition reconciliationCanBeApproved under condition
    partiesAgree = Yes
    and termsNotViolatingLaw = Yes
    and termsNotViolatingOthersRights = Yes
    consequence equals Yes
```

## Article 191. Enforcement of reconciliation terms

```catala
declaration scope Article191ReconciliationEnforcement:
  input reconciliation content ReconciliationProceeding
  input reconciliationApproved content YesNo
  output reconciliationTermsEnforceable content YesNo

scope Article191ReconciliationEnforcement:
  label enforce_default definition reconciliationTermsEnforceable equals No

  label enforce_approved exception enforce_default
  definition reconciliationTermsEnforceable under condition
    reconciliationApproved = Yes
    and reconciliation.result = ReconciliationResult.ReconciliationAccepted
    consequence equals Yes
```
